  "result": "All 5 tests pass, including the two new ones in `tests/test_t2.py`.\n\n**What I changed** in `netgraph/graph.py`, which uses the adjacency-set representation from the spec:\n\n- **`remove_edge(u, v) -> bool`**: discards the edge from both endpoint sets, decrements the edge counter, and returns whether the edge existed. Self-loops work because both endpoints share one set.\n- **`degree(u) -> int`**: returns the size of the node's neighbour set, so a self-loop counts once.\n- **`connected_components()`**: iterative depth-first search over nodes in ascending order. Each component is sorted before being appended, and scanning start nodes in order guarantees components come out ordered by their smallest node.\n\nAll three validate node ids and raise `IndexError` on out-of-range input, matching the existing methods. Nothing under `tests/` was modified, and the changes are uncommitted on the working tree.",
